ents\". Let me list deployments first.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a150aee40e73618d6c552b", "function": {"arguments": "{\"confidence\":0.9,\"service\":\"payments\"}", "name": "list_deployments"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": "The deployment history came back empty. Let me verify the service exists and check its current status.", "reasoning_content": "The payments service has no deployment history. Maybe the service name is wrong \u2014 perhaps \"payments-service\" or something. Let me check service status to see if the service exists.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a150aee6dd764cb18b11a4", "function": {"arguments": "{\"confidence\":0.7,\"service\":\"payments\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": "The service \"payments\" isn't recognized. Let me try common naming variants.", "reasoning_content": "The payments service doesn't exist. Maybe it's named differently, e.g., \"payment\", \"payments-api\", \"payments-service\". I could try a few. Also check incidents list to see if there's context. Let me try common names in parallel.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a150aeeb357279904ee886", "function": {"arguments": "{\"confidence\":0.5,\"service\":\"payments-api\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_01a150aeeb357279904ee887", "function": {"arguments": "{\"confidence\":0.5,\"service\":\"payments-service\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_01a150aeeb357279904ee888", "function": {"arguments": "{\"confidence\":0.4,\"service\":\"payment\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": "Found it: `payments-api` is currently running v5.1.0 in all regions and is unhealthy with an 18% error rate. Now let me get its release history to find the most recent healthy version.", "reasoning_content": "payments-api is the service, unhealthy with 18% error rate. Now get its deployment history to find the last healthy version.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a150aeeec076e387f277d8", "function": {"arguments": "{\"confidence\":0.95,\"service\":\"payments-api\"}", "name": "list_deployments"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": "Release history shows v5.0.0 was healthy and the current v5.1.0 is degraded \u2014 consistent with the errors since this morning's deploy. I'll roll back to v5.0.0 and open the SEV2 incident.", "reasoning_content": "v5.0.0 is the most recent healthy release. Rollback to it. Then create SEV2 incident. Rollback and incident are independent \u2014 can do both in same block? The incident should reference the rollback; independent enough. But maybe safer to do rollback first, confirm success, then incident. They're independent calls though. I'll do both in one block.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a150aef71575e385bb0287", "function": {"arguments": "{\"confidence\":0.95,\"service\":\"payments-api\",\"version\":\"v5.0.0\"}", "name": "rollback"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_01a150aef71575e385bb0288", "function": {"arguments": "{\"confidence\":0.9,\"severity\":\"SEV2\",\"service\":\"payments-api\",\"summary\":\"Since this morning's deployment of v5.1.0, the payments-api has been throwing errors across all production regions (error rate ~18%, service unhealthy). Rolled back all regions to the last healthy release, v5.0.0. Incident opened to track impact and root-cause the v5.1.0 regression.\",\"title\":\"Payments-api degraded after v5.1.0 deploy; rolled back to v5.0.0\"}", "name": "create_incident"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": "Both actions succeeded. Let me verify the rollback restored the service to a healthy state.", "reasoning_content": "Verify rollback restored health.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a150aef9b3758b9f79c594", "function": {"arguments": "{\"confidence\":0.95,\"service\":\"payments-api\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "stop", "content": "All done \u2014 here's a summary:\n\n**Rollback:** The payments service is registered as `payments-api`. Its release history showed v5.0.0 (healthy) followed by this morning's v5.1.0 (degraded, ~18% error rate). I rolled all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) back to **v5.0.0**. Post-rollback verification confirms the service is healthy again with the error rate down to ~0.2%.\n\n**Incident:** Opened **INC-0001** (SEV2) titled \"Payments-api degraded after v5.1.0 deploy; rolled back to v5.0.0\", documenting the degradation, the rollback, and that v5.1.0 needs a root-cause investigation. The on-call engineer has been paged.\n\nOne note: I couldn't open the incident until I identified the correct service name (`payments-api` rather than `payments`), which took a couple of lookup calls.", "reasoning_content": null, "tool_calls": []}]}